{
  "id": "T18_28_adopt_policy_takes_effect_when_made",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "7.7.2",
    "7.7.3",
    "7.7.4",
    "7.6.9",
    "7.6.14",
    "8.4.1",
    "9.5.1",
    "9.5.7",
    "9.5.8"
  ],
  "description": "A change story recorded under the baseline ends at its directive on Friday. An adopt_policy naming the fixture policy, made on Saturday, takes effect when it is made: the period had already ended under the policy then governing, so it keeps the review as its ending at every cutoff, and the fixture policy records no end act for it, even when the directive's expectation is fulfilled on Monday. Reads report the policy governing the unit at the cutoff: the baseline on Friday, the fixture policy from Saturday until a later adopt_policy of the baseline takes effect on Tuesday. Nothing in the story's ending, periods or listings changes, and the transition check is empty.",
  "note": "7.7.3: an `adopt_policy` \"takes effect when it is made, at its context's occurrence time or at `@effective` (8.4.1), and it never rewrites an ending that occurred before then. ... A period that had ended at or before T, under the policy then governing the unit, keeps that ending.\" 7.7.2: \"A read that reports a unit's ending policy reports the one governing it at the cutoff.\" README section 5, Periods: `policy_end` \"is present only when a non-baseline policy governs the unit at some instant of the period\". 7.6.7 (story-held acts): the expectation property begun by the review of chg-1 alone has its acts on chg-1's Item, named as README section 7 states.",
